# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# QA Reviser — environment variables
# Copy to `.env.local` for local dev. Add the same keys in
# Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment Variables.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Supabase (Database) --------------------------------------
# Project → Settings → API
#
# Both are server-only. The app has no login, so the browser never talks to
# Supabase at all: every query runs in a route handler with the service-role
# key. The `anon` key is not used. RLS stays enabled on every table and now
# denies the anon role outright, so a leaked anon key grants nothing.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional: direct Postgres connection string, only needed if you run
# migrations with psql/Prisma instead of the Supabase SQL editor.
DATABASE_URL=

# --- AI (Anthropic Claude) — OPTIONAL -------------------------
# Without it the audit still runs end to end: 25 of the 34 built-in rules
# are deterministic, every link is checked, safe fixes are applied, and the
# report is generated. What you lose is the 9 judgment rules, verification
# of claims against the dealership site, and the written summary. Each of
# those degrades with a recorded warning rather than failing the audit.
# https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Optional override. Defaults to claude-opus-5 (~$0.27 per audit of an
# 8,000-word article). claude-sonnet-5 is ~$0.11 and claude-haiku-4-5 ~$0.05
# for the same work, if cost matters more than judgment quality.
AI_MODEL=claude-opus-5
# Optional: low | medium | high. Defaults to medium (latency-tuned for serverless).
AI_EFFORT=medium

# --- Firecrawl (JS-rendered page fallback) --------------------
# Optional. Without it, pages that need JS rendering are skipped
# with a recorded warning instead of failing the audit.
# https://www.firecrawl.dev/app/api-keys
FIRECRAWL_API_KEY=

# --- Internal job pipeline ------------------------------------
# Shared secret authenticating the self-chaining step requests.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
INTERNAL_JOB_SECRET=

# Secret for the Vercel Cron reaper endpoint.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
CRON_SECRET=

# --- Deployment ------------------------------------------------
# Public origin of the deployment, used to build absolute URLs for the
# self-chaining pipeline. On Vercel this is derived automatically from
# VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL / VERCEL_URL — set it only to override
# (e.g. a custom domain, or local dev on a non-default port).
APP_URL=http://localhost:3000
